cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'To cite package "guluswm" in publications use:'
type: dataset
license: CC-BY-4.0
title: 'guluswm: Household Waste Survey and Characterisation in Gulu City, Uganda'
version: 0.0.0.9000
abstract: 'Field data of a household solid waste study in Gulu City, northern Uganda,
  in September and October 2026: a socio-economic household survey of 424 households
  in six areas of the two city divisions, covering housing, income and expenditure
  bands, waste storage and disposal, the collection service, payment for collection
  and willingness to pay for an improved service, and a seven day waste characterisation
  of 95 households with the weights of 16 sorted fractions, the per capita generation
  rate and the bulk density. The data were collected by Ivan Feni and colleagues of
  Makerere University and Gulu City Council for a manuscript in preparation (Feni,
  Batte, Omal and Niwagaba, 2026). The fieldwork was funded by Integers Company Limited.
  Ivan Feni is the contact for questions about the data.'
